{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"15effd25c041fcd771bb8dc2faa24c6c2856a7423a5780e3c07704c503e79cb8","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot store janitor and GC trigger","key_entities":["src/rebar/_snapshot/gc_trigger.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/__init__.py","src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py","resolve_gate_handle","start_background_janitor","rebar-gate-snapshots","last-pass.stamp","worker.lock","maybe_gc","run_gc","janitor.run_gc","compact_trigger.py","tests/unit/test_snapshot_gc_trigger.py","docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md","docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md"],"problem_keywords":["snapshot store garbage collection","append-only store","resource exhaustion","cadence","operation-linked trigger","single-flight"],"propositions":["Snapshot janitor runs only in the review-bot process, leaving all other hosts with append-only stores that accumulate unbounded disk usage","Non-review-bot hosts (developer laptops, CI runners, library embeds) populate snapshot stores but never reclaim them, causing measured store growth to tens of gigabytes with no reclamation","The fix implements an operation-linked GC trigger that fires on gate-resolution tail for attested handles, using a detached child process to avoid holding store locks on the hot path","The trigger uses a stamped worker-lock sidecar keyed to the snapshot store root and performs an O(1) check against the janitor interval cadence without enumerating the store or acquiring ticket-store locks"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787762918199341001,"uuid":"aabdf89a-ba1d-432b-a4eb-92b21780c948"}